  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds a 15-box pyramid (rows of 5, 4, 3, 2, 1) on a static floor, with each box a dynamic Rapier rigid body. The scene uses the `outdoor-day` look for light and shadows, and the camera is set at an angle so it frames both the pyramid and the ball's path. A heavy sphere launches at the pyramid 1.5 s after the physics starts, with `setVelocity` giving it a speed of about 24 m/s. Space calls `app.setScene(buildScene())` to rebuild the pyramid and ball, then relaunches the ball immediately. The engine owns the render loop. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames. `typecheck` passes. I did not run `vite build` or open the page in a browser, so none of the behaviour has been seen running. The physics needs the optional `@dimforge/rapier3d-compat` package. I couldn't read that folder to confirm it is installed. If it is missing, the page will throw at start-up.",
